  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Ionization energy, in chemistry and physics, the amount of energy required to remove an electron from an isolated atom or molecule. </p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>rd</mi></msup></math> Ionisation energy:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo> </mo><mo>:</mo><mo> </mo><mn>2833</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>mol</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cr</mi><mo>:</mo><mo> </mo><mn>2990</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>mol</mi><mo> </mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Mn</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>3260</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>mol</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Fe</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>2962</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>mol</mi></math></p><p>alternative</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Mn</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>3</mn><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Fe</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>3</mn><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cr</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>3</mn><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>3</mn><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mn>4</mn><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>So <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Mn</mi></math> has highest <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>3</mn><mi>rd</mi></msup><mo> </mo><mi>IE</mi></math> among all the given elements due to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>5</mn></msup></math>configuration</p>"
